   "daf": "17b",
   "sentenceId": 7,
   "he": "וּמִדְּמַאי. דִּתְנַן: מַאֲכִילִין אֶת הָעֲנִיִּים דְּמַאי וְאֶת אַכְסַנְיָא דְּמַאי. אָמַר רַב הוּנָא: תָּנָא, בֵּית שַׁמַּאי אוֹמְרִים: אֵין מַאֲכִילִין אֶת הָעֲנִיִּים דְּמַאי וְאֶת אַכְסַנְיָא דְּמַאי, וּבֵית הִלֵּל אוֹמְרִים: מַאֲכִילִין אֶת הָעֲנִיִּים דְּמַאי וְאֶת אַכְסַנְיָא דְּמַאי.",
   "en": "The mishna continues: «And» in a military camp, one is exempt «from» the separation of tithes from «doubtfully tithed produce [demai]. As we learned» in a mishna: «One may feed the poor demai, and» one may also feed «quartered soldiers [akhsanya] demai. Rav Huna said:» A tanna «taught» in a baraita: «Beit Shammai say» that «one may neither feed the poor demai, nor» may one feed «quartered soldiers demai. And Beit Hillel say» that «one may feed the poor demai, and» one may also feed «quartered soldiers demai.»"
  }
 ],
